     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is well above the labeled maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Order as written:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under physician supervision.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. The risk is high even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing, for example in rheumatologic conditions.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, such as 400 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO twice daily.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed** for analgesia or antipyresis.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and give the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note documenting that the dose was intentional. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to enter."
      }
     ],
